{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>For the soul of the flesh, it is in the blood.</b> With a hirek (chirik vowel) — the first and last [words] are read as feminine forms, and the two middle ones as masculine forms, as they are written. And a mnemonic for the matter: נקבה תסובב גבר (a woman surrounds a man)." "<b>It shall make atonement for the soul.</b> On account of the soul it shall make atonement."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {0 "The comment addresses the vocalization and gender of the four words נפש הבשר בדם הוא; the mnemonic appears to be a play indicating that feminine forms enclose masculine ones, though its precise force is obscure."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:13:09.879136848Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}